          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>During thyroidectomy, injury to the recurrent laryngeal nerve causes hoarseness </p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>During thyroidectomy, injury to the recurrent laryngeal nerve causes hoarseness because this nerve:</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Tenses the vocal cord for high-pitched phonation</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Vocal cord tensing is the function of the cricothyroid muscle, which is supplied by the external laryngeal nerve, not the recurrent laryngeal nerve.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Innervates all intrinsic laryngeal muscles except the cricothyroid</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. The recurrent laryngeal nerve controls all intrinsic laryngeal muscles except the cricothyroid. Loss of this innervation impairs vocal cord movement, causing hoarseness.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Provides sensory innervation to the supraglottic larynx</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Supraglottic sensation is carried by the internal laryngeal nerve, a branch of the superior laryngeal nerve — not the recurrent laryngeal nerve.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Constricts the inferior thyroid artery during phonation</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The recurrent laryngeal nerve is a motor nerve to the laryngeal muscles. It does not innervate blood vessels.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Review the two nerve-artery pairs: the superior thyroid artery travels with the external laryngeal nerve (cricothyroid), and the inferior thyroid artery crosses near the recurrent laryngeal nerve (all other intrinsic laryngeal muscles)."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "The recurrent laryngeal nerve runs close to the inferior thyroid artery — the key surgical relationship to remember during thyroidectomy."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
